    "global_summary": "A Joint Works Agreement is a structured legal contract between multiple water license holders or land occupants who jointly construct and manage shared water infrastructure. It defines the parties involved, their water rights, cost-sharing percentages, operational responsibilities, governance through a manager, usage restrictions, land access rights, dispute resolution mechanisms, and legal continuity. It ensures coordinated development and maintenance of shared water systems while preventing misuse and defining enforceable obligations for all parties.",
