            "title": "Purpose of Joint Works Agreement",
            "content": "A Joint Works Agreement is a legal document used when multiple parties jointly construct, operate, and maintain shared infrastructure such as water diversion or irrigation systems. It defines ownership, responsibilities, cost-sharing, usage limits, and dispute resolution procedures.",
